62. DRAWING GENERATION POLICY
The system shall distinguish:
DESIGN_DRAWING
COORDINATION_DRAWING
VALIDATION_DRAWING
PERMIT_DOCUMENTATION
FINAL_DOCUMENT_PACKAGE
Not every drawing operation requires the same validation gate.
Final permit-oriented documentation requires the strictest configured gate.

63. DOCUMENTATION COORDINATION VALIDATION
Before final document generation, the engine shall verify:
model ↔ view
view ↔ drawing
drawing ↔ sheet
sheet ↔ revision
schedule ↔ model
annotation ↔ object
dimension ↔ geometry
Broken documentation references shall produce validation results.

64. SCHEDULE VALIDATION
Schedules shall be validated against the project model.
Examples:
door schedule count = model door count
window schedule count = model window count
room schedule count = model room count
Discrepancies shall be reported.

65. DRAWING COORDINATION
The engine shall identify discrepancies such as:
plan shows door
schedule does not contain door

plan shows window
elevation does not reflect window

section cuts through object
section annotation references missing object

room number differs between plan and schedule
These become document coordination results.

66. SHEET COMPLETENESS
A final sheet set shall be checked for:
required sheets
sheet numbers
drawing titles
revision information
project information
scale
north indication where applicable
required notes
required schedules
required legends

67. FINAL PACKAGE VALIDATION
Before document-package finalization:
MODEL_GATE = PASS
GEOMETRY_GATE = PASS
COMPLIANCE_GATE = PASS or configured REVIEW state
DOCUMENTATION_GATE = PASS
The exact acceptance policy is project-configurable.
Critical failures shall remain blocking unless explicitly resolved through the appropriate project workflow.

